        <type><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_encrypted_chunk_store_1_1_encrypt_result" kindref="compound">EncryptResult</ref></type>
        <definition>EncryptedChunkStore::EncryptResult themis::EncryptedChunkStore::encryptChunk</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;series_id, const std::vector&lt; uint8_t &gt; &amp;plaintext, const std::string &amp;chunk_range=&quot;&quot;)</argsstring>
        <name>encryptChunk</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::EncryptedChunkStore::encryptChunk</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>series_id</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::vector&lt; uint8_t &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>plaintext</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>chunk_range</declname>
          <defval>&quot;&quot;</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Encrypt a Gorilla-compressed binary chunk. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Derives a DEK from the current master key and the series_id via HKDF-SHA256, then encrypts <computeroutput>plaintext</computeroutput> with AES-256-GCM.</para>
<para>The returned <ref refid="structthemis_1_1_encrypted_chunk_store_1_1_encrypt_result" kindref="compound">EncryptResult</ref> contains the ciphertext blob <bold>and</bold> the key_id actually used during encryption. Always use the returned key_id (not <ref refid="classthemis_1_1_encrypted_chunk_store_1af9299d2fa8ef2e280eef64dc3d27a2e5" kindref="member">getCurrentKeyId()</ref>) when persisting the JSON envelope to guarantee consistency even if the master key rotates during the call.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>series_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>&quot;{metric}:{entity}&quot; string used as HKDF salt. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>plaintext</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Raw Gorilla-compressed bytes to encrypt. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>chunk_range</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Human-readable range string &quot;[first_ts,last_ts]&quot; written to the audit log. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_encrypted_chunk_store_1_1_encrypt_result" kindref="compound">EncryptResult</ref> with the ciphertext blob and the key_id embedded in the blob header. </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::runtime_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>on OpenSSL or key-provider failure. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
